@required 'stdlib';

/*
`fix var := expr` is a way to create a recursive structure.

`fix var := expr` is equivalent to:
```onion
var := mut undefined;
var = expr;
```
So the `fix point` is always mutable.

Here, `A` is defined as a tuple containing itself and the integer `1`.
When we print `A`, it will show the recursive structure as `(..., 1)`, indicating that `A` contains itself.
*/
fix A := (A, 1);

stdlib.io.println(A);

fix M := fix N := (M, (N, 42));

stdlib.io.println(M);
